request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (Changing a field in the shared types unit affects every unit that imports it. So types gets the new declaration, and format, storage and commands are told what they will receive and switch from done to completed. Behaviour stays the same otherwise. ListOptions.includeDone stays as it is, since the request only covers the Todo field.)
round 1: owners types=rejected format=rejected storage=rejected commands=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (All four owners were rejected only because their test fixtures had to change from `done` to `completed`, which is exactly what the rename requires. I'm approving those four test changes and sending the same plan again.)
round 2: owners types=ok format=ok storage=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (Type-checking and tests both pass (16 tests, 0 failed). The manifest shows Todo now has `completed: boolean` instead of `done`, and all four units were updated to use it. The only test changes were the approved fixture renames from `done` to `completed`; test titles and expected values stayed the same. ListOptions.includeDone was kept on purpose because it's a list option, not the Todo field. One thing to note: todo JSON files saved before this change still have `done`, and nothing converts them to `completed`.)

